From e66dc073d931703be76da84dfb7f4a2c9c73d8a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Goueslain <nicolas.goueslain@nxp.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 19:03:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Ara-2 NPU tensor_filter with V2 API and DMA-BUF support

This commit adds support for Kinara Ara-2 NPU hardware acceleration on
NXP i.MX platforms (i.MX 8M Plus, i.MX 95) via a new tensor_filter
sub-plugin that implements the V2 framework API.

Updates:
========

1. V2 Framework API
   - Added GST_TENSOR_FILTER_FRAMEWORK_V2 with DMA-BUF support
   - invoke_v2() callback receives GstMemory* for zero-copy inference
   - propose_allocation() enables custom buffer pool negotiation
   - get_output_quantization() propagates quantization parameters
   - Backward compatible with existing V0/V1 sub-plugins

2. Ara-2 NPU Tensor Filter (tensor_filter_ara2.cc)
   - Three-tier invoke strategy:
     a) Zero-copy from pre-allocated DMA-BUF pool
     b) Extract DMA-BUF fd from upstream GstMemory
     c) CPU fallback with memory mapping
   - Runtime dlopen of libaraclient_aarch64.so for graceful degradation
   - Custom NnsAra2DmaBufInputPool for buffer allocation
   - Communicates with dvproxy daemon via Unix socket

3. Tensor Quantization Metadata
   - Added GstNnsTensorQuantMeta for quantization parameter propagation
   - Enables proper dequantization in downstream elements
   - Attached to output buffers via GstMeta system

Dependencies:
=============
Build-time:
  - dvapi.h header (from imx-nxp-ara2 package)
  - gstreamer1.0-plugins-base (for gst-allocators)
Runtime:
  - libaraclient_aarch64.so (dlopen'd from imx-nxp-ara2)
  - dvproxy daemon (systemd service)
  - kernel-module-uiodma (recommended for DMA operations)

Platform Support:
=================
- NXP i.MX 8M Plus with Kinara Ara-2 PCIe card
- NXP i.MX 95 with Kinara Ara-2 PCIe card

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [i.MX specific]

Signed-off-by: Nicolas Goueslain <nicolas.goueslain@nxp.com>
